Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:06:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] generalized-bulletproofs: test that the prover's output
 is unchanged, byte for byte

A fixed-seed test for the memory changes that follow. It builds 8 circuits
with vector commitments, as fuzz_test_arithmetic_circuit does, using a
deterministic RNG (Blake2b-512 of a seed and a counter, defined in the test).
For each circuit it proves, verifies, and compares the proofs' bytes with
tests/data/prove_unchanged.hex.

The expected bytes were made by the prover of monerodato.3. In that file the
prover is the same as upstream's. The following commits only move, shrink and
free buffers in ArithmeticCircuitStatement::prove, so the bytes must not
change.

Checked before committing, in a crate copy of the .3 tag's patched/:
- the test passes on .3's prover;
- it passes with the three memory changes applied;
- it fails under a mutation that changes the proofs but keeps them valid
  (sL and sR drawn in swapped order).

GBP_WRITE_PROVE_UNCHANGED=1 rewrites the file from the current code. Use it
only from a prover known to be unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
